  <reason>Subject and account: The subject of this report is Bilal Imtiaz, holder of account PK**BAHL****1759, opened on 28 August 2023. The customer's declared occupation is medical sales officer (salaried), with a declared income of PKR 120,000 per month.

Activity summary: During the period 2 April 2026 to 25 April 2026, the account recorded 12 credits totalling PKR 17,802,000 as well as 4 debits totalling PKR 15,499,000. The credits included 11 cash deposits totalling PKR 17,682,000, made over the counter at 4 branches (Clifton Branch, DHA Phase 6 Branch, Gulshan-e-Iqbal Branch, Saddar Branch). The activity was detected on 25 April 2026, when Tazama typology STR-PK-01 scored 320 against an alert threshold of 300.

Grounds for suspicion: 9 of 11 cash deposits (82%) were between PKR 1,600,000 and PKR 1,999,999, totalling PKR 15,843,000, just below the cash transaction reporting threshold of PKR 2,000,000. The cash was deposited across 4 branches (Clifton Branch, DHA Phase 6 Branch, Gulshan-e-Iqbal Branch, Saddar Branch) rather than at a single branch. Credits in the activity window were 148.3 times the declared monthly income, against a declared income of PKR 120,000 per month. Taken together, these indicators are consistent with suspected structuring; the reporting entity has not established the underlying offence.

Flow of funds: Of the outgoing funds, PKR 15,499,000 was sent to Crescent Imports (PK**CRES****1592, Synthetic Bank B) in 4 transactions. Funds did not remain in the account: debits equal to 87% of credits, with a median of 26.1 hours between the latest credit and each debit.

Other considerations: Screening of the subject returned no match on sanctions, PEP or adverse-media screening on 28 April 2026.

Action taken by the reporting entity: Action taken: a note by L2 analyst (28 April 2026): "Account placed under enhanced monitoring pending the reporting decision. No contact made with the customer about this review."</reason>
